WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.570
- Thanks to CuriosityStream

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.503
for keeping Legal Eagle in the air.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.400
(thunder cracks)

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.210
He gently pulls the chair
away and grabs the doorknob.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.800
He turns.
(doorknob rattles)

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.743
He pulls.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.780
Oddly, there's slight resistance,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.030
then he yanks the door

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.123
and Katko's life and
limbs are changed forever.

00:00:22.123 --> 00:00:24.960
(door slams)
(man yells)

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.870
A man's house is his castle.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.080
It's the place we feel safe.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.310
It's the place we raise our children,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.200
and it's the place we keep
our most precious belongings.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.770
But to what lengths may we go to protect

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.340
our personal property and our home?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.208
When is deadly force justified?

00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:47.999
That's the question we must answer in

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:51.571
The Case of the Shotgun Booby Trap.

00:00:51.571 --> 00:00:53.840
(dramatic music)

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.900
Submitted for adjudication.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.320
Our story begins with a gift.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.220
The year is 1957, the place
an isolated farm house

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.020
in Mahaska County, Iowa.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.020
On this day, Edward and Bertha Briney

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.170
are thrilled to learn that
they're about to inherit

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.950
a fertile eight-acre farm
from Bertha's parents,

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.520
the shining gem amidst the
rolling golden wheat fields,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.610
a farm house, a symbol
of the American pioneer.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:23.210
The couple is elated,
they dream of passing on

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.100
their property to their
children and grandchildren.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.750
Little do they know that
this quaint little home

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.790
in the heartland is about to
throw their lives into chaos.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.330
Although they love the farm house,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.720
Ed and Bertha do not live there.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.060
Instead they reside in
another home outside of town.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.940
They try their best to secure
the inherited property,

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.320
especially to protect the antiques

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.690
and heirlooms stored within.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.970
Unfortunately, the
Brineys grow increasingly

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.980
unable to care for the farm house,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.160
and it begins to deteriorate
faster than they can repair.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.190
Both time and weather batter the house.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.594
The harsh midwestern winters
strip the paint off the boards,

00:02:03.594 --> 00:02:08.490
crack the windows like broken
teeth, and cave the roof in.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:12.120
The home becomes dilapidated
and the Brineys are frustrated.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.210
The gift starts to seem
less like a blessing

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.430
and more like a curse.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.850
They have no idea how right they are.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.663
Worse yet, the farm house
is isolated and vulnerable,

00:02:24.663 --> 00:02:28.610
like a haunted house
beset by troubled ghosts.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.530
There are no nearby neighbors
to protect the home,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.770
and it becomes ripe for looting.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.590
As the years pass,
Bertha's family heirlooms

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.450
start disappearing, stolen
by a persistent swarm

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.400
of criminals and thieves.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.040
A series of trespassing and
house-breaking incidents

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.060
inflict more damage to the property,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.060
and soon nearly everything
that Bertha treasured is gone,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.840
stolen by looters that
seem to worm their way in

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.833
to the house like locusts, and
like locusts, strip it bare.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.390
Angry and despondent, the
Brineys post keep out signs

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.520
and install locks, but all is in vain.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.280
For a decade, Ed Briney
listens to his wife's pleas

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.370
as she begs him to do something.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.899
Meanwhile, on the other side of town,

00:03:15.899 --> 00:03:19.330
a couple of buddies are up to no good.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:23.070
Meet one Marvin Katko, a
married gas station attendant

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.170
barely able to make ends meet.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.230
He's been in and out of work for weeks

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.630
and is looking for some quick cash.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.270
And meet Katko's soon-to-be
partner in crime,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.780
Marvin McDonough, who has heard
about the Briney residence

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.350
and the easy money to be made there.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.110
McDonough convinces Katko
that grabbing some antiques

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.140
could earn them a pretty penny,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.260
and Katko is just
desperate enough to agree.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.910
Before long, the two conspirators break in

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.930
and steal some antique bottles
and jars for preserves.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.543
Their little heist proves fruitful.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.920
Finally, something snaps in
the mind of Edward Briney.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.790
Fed up with the looting
and wanton destruction,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.060
Briney cleans and oils
his 20 gauge shotgun,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.270
and he climbs the flight
of groaning stairs

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.920
for the second floor bedroom.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.700
A desperate plan takes shape in his mind.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.850
He ignores the uneasy feeling
in the pit of his stomach.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.870
He is a man who has had enough.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.040
Fury pulsing in his veins,

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.031
Briney enters the north bedroom.

00:04:22.031 --> 00:04:25.010
Working by the light of
the late afternoon sun,

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.860
he secures the shotgun to
the foot of the iron bed wire

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.020
and runs another wire from the trigger

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.110
to the bedroom doorknob.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.660
He crouches, adjusting the shotgun's aim,

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.380
leveling it straight at the
middle of the door frame

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.020
where it is sure to hit
the thief in the abdomen,

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.390
a death sentence, and then he
calls downstairs to Bertha.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:49.800
When Bertha sees Ed's booby
trap, she has only one qualm.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.040
She doesn't want the
would-be thief to get shot

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.920
in the stomach, so Bertha
convinces Ed to lower the gun

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.750
and to point it at the
bottom of the door instead.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.120
Ed agrees and adjusts the shotgun.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.010
He nails a piece of tin over the window

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.600
to prevent anyone from seeing the trap.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.600
He loads the gun, cocks the
trigger, and closes the door.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.380
Bertha shoves a chair
under the door's knob

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.230
as one last signal to thieves

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.180
that the bedroom isn't meant to be opened.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.300
At last, the Brineys leave,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.320
knowing the next person to open the door

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.333
is in for a horrifying shock.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.736
Meanwhile, high off of their first haul,

00:05:26.736 --> 00:05:29.400
Katko and McDonough decide to go back,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.380
reasoning there must be more in the rooms

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:32.740
that they haven't opened yet.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.100
So the two tiptoe back
onto the Brineys' land

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.670
under cover of darkness, but this time,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:41.350
unbeknownst to them, they
face a bloody reckoning.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.720
Katko and McDonough pry loose a board

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.420
from a back porch window.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.690
They break and enter.
(glass shatters)

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.820
Once inside the house, Katko
goes straight to the bedrooms

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.630
while McDonough searches downstairs.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.940
He enters the hallway, no one is home,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.610
but he's careful to avoid excessive noise.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.610
The old floor boards creak
with each heavy step.

00:06:03.851 --> 00:06:07.390
Katko notices a chair under
the north bedroom door.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.807
Strange, but no matter.

00:06:09.807 --> 00:06:14.070
He gently pulls the chair
away and grabs the doorknob.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.600
He turns, he pulls.
(doorknob rattles)

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.260
Oddly, there's slight resistance,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.850
then he yanks the door,
(door creaks)

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.725
and Katko's life and
limbs are changed forever.

00:06:24.725 --> 00:06:26.020
(gun fires)
(man yells)

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.750
The sound of the blast
is deafening, it's chaos.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.080
Katko drops, one of his legs a bloody mess

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.050
of tissue and bone splinters,

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.680
the sickly sweet smell of
gunpowder fills the air,

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.240
adding to the pandemonium.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.940
Katko screams in agony and
McDonough rushes to the bedroom.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.960
He stares in dumbstruck horror,

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.413
Katko lies there writing.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.360
McDonough lifts his friend on his shoulder

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.650
and half-carries him
down to the front yard.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.710
From there, McDonough helps
as much as he can as Katko

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.380
crawls the seemingly endless
distance to the car where

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.600
the two finally rush through
the night to the hospital.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.230
There, after doctors stop the bleeding,

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.160
they explain to Katko and his wife

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:05.410
that he needs three to four weeks of care

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.470
before the hospital can discharge him.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.920
Katko has lost a substantial
amount of bone and tissue,

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.650
and his leg needs to be amputated,
but almost miraculously,

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.550
Katko barely avoids that horrible step.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:21.470
Yet Katko's injury doesn't
prevent the law from swooping in.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.690
After a 40-day stay in the hospital,

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.790
Katko faces the police who arrest him

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:28.040
on breaking and entering
and larceny charges.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:33.000
Katko pays a fine of $50 and
serves a 60-day jail sentence

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.400
until he is paroled for good behavior.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.580
Except for this, Katko's record is clean.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.100
But this man's ordeal is far from over.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.190
He suffers a full year in a cast

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.580
and another year in a special brace.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.350
He wrestles with pain and
knows he will walk with a limp

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.150
for the rest of his life.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.639
Katko knows he was committing a crime,

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:56.735
but the longer he sits, his
leg throbbing like torture,

00:07:56.735 --> 00:08:00.920
the more he convinces himself
that he doesn't deserve this.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.962
This isn't fair.

00:08:02.962 --> 00:08:05.940
Something breaks in Katko's mind.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.728
Like Briney before him, Katko
decides he wants justice.

00:08:10.728 --> 00:08:13.570
(gun fires)
(tense music)

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.000
Katko served his time in jail

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.470
and paid his debt to society,

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.800
which brought the criminal
side of this case to a close.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.760
But once out of jail,
Katko wanted compensation

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:25.348
for his gruesome shotgun injuries.

00:08:25.348 --> 00:08:29.140
So like a true American, Katko filed suit.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.080
That's right, the thief
sued the homeowner.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:33.730
Katko claimed that his leg injury

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.270
resulted from unreasonable
force by the Brineys

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:38.830
to protect their personal
property by setting up

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.780
a spring gun, AKA a shotgun booby trap.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.593
Needless to say, Ed and
Bertha Briney were furious.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.290
The case went all the way up
to the Iowa Supreme Court.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.940
The issue, whether setting up a spring gun

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:54.830
in an uninhabited house is considered

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.640
reasonable force for
protection of property.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.240
In other words, was
Edward allowed to set up

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.010
a shotgun booby trap to
protect his house and home?

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.120
Remember, the house was unoccupied

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.500
at the time of the break-in.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.723
So how far does the right
to self defense actually go?

00:09:11.723 --> 00:09:13.710
We take you to the court house,

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.600
where the argument between
the lawyers for each side

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.003
is about to begin.

00:09:18.003 --> 00:09:20.490
(typewriter clicks)

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.150
- [Judge] Good morning, this
court has had an opportunity

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:26.100
to review the record, the parties' briefs.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.090
Are counselors ready
to begin oral argument?

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:30.590
- [Bruce] Yes, your Honor, Bruce Palmer

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.460
representing appellants
Mr. and Mrs. Briney.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:35.370
- [Lawyer] Yes Justice, Geri Heslinga

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.330
for Mr. Katko, appellee.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:39.600
- [Judge] All right then, let's proceed.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.160
Mr. Palmer, what do you have to say?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.510
- [Bruce] Thank you, and
may it please the court,

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.830
it is frankly a miscarriage of justice

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.900
that an admitted thief
would seek monetary damages

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.440
from the homeowners he tried to burgle.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.790
My clients, Edward and Bertha
Briney, did everything right.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.220
They followed the law,
setting up a mere deterrent

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:01.080
in their unoccupied home,
a home which was clearly

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.200
not meant for guests,
especially trespassing intruders

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.550
with intent to burglarize the home.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:09.300
For 10 years, the Brineys
repeatedly installed locks

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.880
and posted many No Trespassing signs,

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.880
boarded up windows, and even
desperately sought assistance

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.400
from the Sheriff's department,

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.920
but none of these efforts
prevented continuous

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.420
break-ins and thefts to
the family's heirloom home.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.550
Katko, the thief, had no right

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.910
to even set foot on the Brineys' land.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.800
- [Geri] Your Honor, the
key to deciding this case

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:31.000
is the oldest legal question on the books.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.850
Does the punishment fit the crime?

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.040
The obvious answer here is no.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.710
The Constitution itself
prohibits cruel and unusual

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.600
punishment in criminal cases,

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.870
but it also makes sense in
a civil case like this one.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.430
My client admitted he was
guilty of breaking and entering

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.420
and larceny in the nighttime,
but he was arrested.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:51.300
He served his time and he
paid the required fine.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:54.360
He paid his debt to
society and the Brineys.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.060
Yes, the Brineys had a right
to protect their property,

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:59.540
but to the extent of
ruining a decent man's life

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.520
by blowing off one of his legs?

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.100
- [Bruce] All the Brineys
intended with the spring gun

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:06.510
in the bedroom was to scare intruders.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.430
They had no desire or intention

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.720
to seriously maim or kill anyone.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.567
Katko, while he tries to play the

00:11:12.567 --> 00:11:15.510
"oops I made a little mistake"
card, actually carefully

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.440
planned the burglary to
steal the Brineys' valuables

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.570
and sell them for his own benefit.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.450
He's a convict, a repeat offender,

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:26.500
and had no right to expect
warmth or safety in a vacant home

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.200
which he knew had been
repeatedly vandalized.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.070
Imagine if he seriously cut himself

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.340
while breaking one of
the farm house windows.

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:35.870
That could be just as
dangerous as a shotgun,

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:38.320
but we would all agree that the Brineys

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.920
would not be liable for his injuries then.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.280
This situation is exactly the same.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:48.580
Katko's injuries resulted
from his own bad decisions.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.940
- [Geri] Oh that's going too far.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.310
My client not only suffered
the horrendous injury

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.930
at the time the shotgun
blew off much of his bone

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.730
and leg tissue, but almost
had his leg amputated,

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.770
needed crutches and a special brace

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:02.220
for almost two years and still suffers

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.560
substantial pain to this very day,

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:07.510
all because he attempted to
take a few antique bottles

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.943
to sell so he could keep himself
and his wife above water.

00:12:10.943 --> 00:12:13.546
- [Judge] I appreciate
your arguments, counselors,

00:12:13.546 --> 00:12:15.480
but the law is clear.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.540
The relevant question for the court

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.770
is whether the actions of
the Brineys was reasonable.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:24.050
Now Katko did not have
permission to enter the premises

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.760
and did not have permission to steal

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.890
the Brineys' belongings,
that much is clear.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.410
However, as a society, we
don't want people setting up

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:36.890
shotgun booby traps or planting
landmines in their yards.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.890
- [Geri] Your Honor, any
reasonable person knows

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:42.350
the terrible damage a shotgun
can do a point-blank range.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:44.730
Indeed, the fact that the
Brineys lowered the aim

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.920
of the gun is an admission of that fact.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.810
Thus, they obviously
intended to grievously harm

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:51.820
the next person to open that door.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.440
In this case, it was poor Mr. Katko.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.020
- [Judge] Mr. Palmer, do you think

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.430
the Brineys' trap was reasonable?

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.400
- [Bruce] I do, your Honor.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.250
Was it reasonable for them to be upset

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.880
and want to prevent
further break-ins, yes.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.810
Did they try less drastic
measures to accomplish their goal

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.380
prior to the spring gun, yes.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:13.280
Did those measures stop the
stealing and vandalism, no.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:15.350
Does it make sense for them to have taken

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.490
a more extreme measure, yes.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.530
Your Honor, you called it a trap,

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:22.080
but that implies that
it was out in the wild

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.730
and that anyone walking in public

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:26.060
could have come within
the sights of the shotgun,

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:29.810
but the Brineys were careful
to only protect their own home

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:32.700
and place their deterrent
in their own bedroom.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.930
- [Geri] Your Honor, the
flaw in the Brineys' argument

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.300
is clear, what if it had been someone else

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.710
that opened the door that night?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.920
What if some young boys out for a walk

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.820
had decided to explore the dark home

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.520
as an adventure, as children sometimes do?

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:49.100
What if the boys, having no
plan to steal or vandalize,

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:50.880
had wandered through the home and then,

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:54.570
in one awful blast, a
child's life had been lost?

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.770
Clearly, the death of
an innocent young child

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.990
would not be reasonable just
to protect some property.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:01.460
What else can we conclude?

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.500
The hidden gun trap was
intended to catch someone by

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:08.500
surprise and cause a devastating
personal injury or worse.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.920
Imagine a person on trial
for attempted murder

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.550
and claiming that it couldn't be murder

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.500
because he only aimed for
someone's non-vital organs?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.500
Preposterous, if my client
had not been accompanied

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.000
by his friend, he would
have bled to death.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.870
The Brineys were out for
blood and they got it.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.560
Now it's on their hands.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:27.460
My client simply wants compensation

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.350
for the damage that they did to him.

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:31.250
- [Judge] Are we to
suggest that a homeowner

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:34.190
can never use deadly
force to protect his home?

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.480
Is that the precedent you want to set?

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.080
Mr. Palmer, under what
circumstances, if any,

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.780
is a spring gun a legally permitted device

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.780
for protection of personal property?

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.310
- [Bruce] Your Honor, the law is settled

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.870
that property owners may
use substantial force,

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:50.930
even spring guns and shotguns,

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:54.110
to protect their property
under certain circumstances,

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:57.250
including a home invasion,
especially at night.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.040
Who's to say the Briney
family was not protecting

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.780
a dwelling where Mrs. Briney

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.230
may be spending time on her own?

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.840
She has a right to protect her
own life with deadly force,

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.210
so the only unreasonable matter here

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:13.590
is Katko's asking this
court to award him money

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:16.837
for an injury he sustained
by illegally entering a home

00:15:16.837 --> 00:15:20.530
where the homeowner might have
been dwelling at the time.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.540
- [Geri] Your Honor, opposing
counsel conveniently omits

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.660
that part of the
well-settled law that says

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.700
spring guns or other mechanical devices

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.630
installed to cause serious
bodily harm or death

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.440
may only be used if the
homeowner is present

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.670
in the dwelling while the trap is set.

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.290
We may not like the reason
Mr. Katko was there,

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.000
but his status as a
trespasser shouldn't justify

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.770
homeowners throughout the country

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.870
rigging firearms to
shoot anyone at any time.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:48.150
- [Judge] Thank you, I
think I've heard enough.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:50.480
Any closing remarks, Mr. Palmer?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.500
- [Bruce] Thank you,
while it was mere property

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.210
my clients were protecting,

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.300
these were belongings in a home where

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.600
Mrs. Briney frequently spent time,

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.450
thus this case should be looked upon

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:05.250
as one in which the law
permits use of a spring gun.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.590
It might be different if the belongings

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.810
were in a shack or a
barn, but they were not.

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:13.630
It was merely luck that the
Brineys were not present

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.340
at the time of the home invasion.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:19.466
Yet Mr. Katko sees to punish
the Brineys for the good

00:16:19.466 --> 00:16:22.650
fortune that they were not
home at the time he broke in.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.820
- [Geri] Not withstanding
counsel's seemingly sound

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:28.900
argument, it is completely
unsupported by actual Iowa law.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.980
Any reasonable person would have realized

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.630
that a 20 gauge shotgun precariously wired

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.670
to fire into a doorway,
any part of a doorway,

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:40.450
could cause serious bodily
harm or death to an entrant.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.760
Thus the spring gun set up by the Brineys

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.840
was legally impermissible.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:47.850
- [Judge] Thank you, counselors,
this matter is adjourned.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:50.597
I will return soon with
the court's decision.

00:16:50.597 --> 00:16:53.920
(typewriter clicks)

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.450
- Justice Moore wrote the decision

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:58.990
of the Iowa Supreme Court
in February of 1971,

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.610
and the precedent that it set is still

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:03.390
the law of the land in
Iowa and many states today.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.340
Pause this video and let
me know in the comments

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.624
how you think this case came out.

00:17:07.624 --> 00:17:10.930
(typewriter clicks)
(relaxed music)

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:13.510
The Iowa Supreme Court
held that the rule of law

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.420
to be applied was this: one may, in fact,

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.380
use reasonable force to
protect mere property,

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.420
but a homeowner may not
use a means of force

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:25.379
that will take human life or
inflict great bodily harm.

00:17:25.379 --> 00:17:27.870
The fact that a trespasser may be acting

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:30.870
in violation of the law
doesn't change that rule,

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.900
and the only time the
setting of a spring gun

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.840
is justified is if a
trespasser is committing

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:39.440
a felony of violence or
one punishable by death,

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:43.710
or where a trespasser is
endangering human life by his act.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:47.221
In other words, the
Brineys, the homeowners,

00:17:47.221 --> 00:17:49.008
were in the wrong.

00:17:49.008 --> 00:17:52.700
It was unlawful to set up
their spring gun booby trap,

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.610
and what happened to the Brineys?

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:58.160
Well hold on to your hats,
the jury's verdict for Katko

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:01.520
and against the Brineys
awarded Katko $20,000

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:05.816
for actual damages plus another
$10,000 in punitive damages.

00:18:05.816 --> 00:18:08.810
The jury found that
the Brineys' booby trap

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.420
was so heinous that the
couple should not only

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:15.230
pay for the actual
damages but also $10,000

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:16.440
just to punish them.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.550
So was it fair or unfair that
a trespasser attempting to

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:23.130
burglarize your house has
any protections at all?

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:25.590
It's difficult to disagree that human life

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.870
is more important than property,

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.430
no matter how sentimental the items.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:31.860
But what do you think?

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:34.430
The case of the shotgun
booby trap is the first

